==English==
===Etymology===
{{L.}} [[post]], ''[[afterwards]]'' + [[mortem]] from [[mors]], ''[[death]]''
===Adjective===
'''post mortem'''
# occurring after death
===Noun===
{{en-noun}} (abbreviated as ''[[PM]]'')
# An [[investigation]] of a [[corpse]] to determine the cause of [[death]]; an [[autopsy]]

# Metaphorically any investigation after something considered unsecessfull, especially used of meetings and bridge games.  ''See also'': [[drains up]].

===Expression===

# After death.
#: The injuries were found to have been caused ''post-mortem''.

===Alternative spellings===
*postmortem
*post-mortem
